  "id": "COMPOUND:40214 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (5R,6R,7aR)-6-ethenyl-7a-hydroxy-3,6-dimethyl-5-prop-1-en-2-yl-5,7-dihydro-4H-1-benzofuran-2-one and FaDu, the human fetal duodenal epithelial cell line. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which point to the compound as a target for Phosphodiesterase 6C. Phosphodiesterase 6C is known to be a target of both Alpha-Humulene Epoxide and another compound, (8R,21S)-16,27-dimethoxy-7,22-dimethyl-29,31,33-trioxa-7,22-diazaoctacyclo[19.11.3.14,32.110,14.115,19.03,8.025,35.028,34]octatriaconta-1(32),2,4(36),10(38),11,13,15,17,19(37),25,27,34-dodecaen-13-ol, which itself has a target of FaDu. The consistent involvement of Phosphodiesterase 6C across these pathways indicates a possible mechanism by which the compound may interact with FaDu. The evidence is strong and consistent, suggesting that the compound may act as a modulator of Phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially influencing cellular processes in FaDu. The relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, which collectively provide a robust foundation for the proposed interaction.",
